<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tarragona</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tarragona is a port city in Catalonia, north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, capital of the province of the same name. Built on the Roman city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarraco">Tarraco</a>, it was held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a>, largely abandoned after the Muslim conquest, and restored in the 12th century as the seat of a Catalan archbishopric. Its archbishop still heads an ecclesiastical province, and its Roman remains are a World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tarragona.jpg" alt="Tarragona" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bernard Gagnon · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roman_circus_of_Tarraco_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
